A truncheon is the old-fashioned simple short club.

A police baton (in USAnian usage, a "nightstick") is a two-foot-long rod
of hard plastic, usually with a handle sticking out at 90 degrees to the
shaft near one end.  It's a better weapon than a wooden truncheon (being
longer), and can also be used as a forearm guard with which to block
knives and such.
